okf.py is a derived work, modified from the upstream source noted below. Every
modification is listed in the file's own header.

  okf.py             <- src/reference_agent/bundle/document.py

Summary of changes:
  * The Python package was collapsed into one module, okf.py.
  * A `validate` subcommand was added; upstream ships no conformance checker.
  * Link extraction resolves bundle-absolute (`/`-prefixed) links and ignores
    links inside code spans and fences.
  * `log.md` is excluded from the concept walk.
  * Timestamp parsing accepts a trailing `Z` on Python 3.10.

The `visualize` subcommand and the viewer assets it derived from upstream
(viewer/generator.py, viewer/templates/viz.html, viewer/static/viz.css,
viewer/static/viz.js) and the libraries it vendored (Cytoscape.js, marked) were
**removed** — see /decisions/delivery-standalone-app.md. Only the validator, and
the document loader it shares, remain derived from the reference agent.
